  # These edits are text substitutions, so a block this kit CHANGED between
  # versions would be inserted a second time: the syntax check catches that and
  # reverts, and the old block then stays installed forever, repeating the same
  # failure on every start. (The frontend needs none of this -- it always rebuilds
  # its patched copy from the bundle upstream shipped.)
  #
  # Self-healing across package upgrades, with no version to keep track of:
  # upstream never says KIT, so a file that does not is the original -- cache it.
